meta {
  name: 15. Cleanup - Delete DataSet (safety net)
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{sqlDataSetId}}
}

tests {
  test("DataSet already gone or deleted", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // After the DELETE saga (steps 12/13) the dataset entity is already removed → 404.
    // 204 only occurs as a safety net for a never-provisioned run deleted synchronously.
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **SQL saga step 15** — Delete the dataset (safety net).

  With the new delete contract this step is normally a no-op: the DATASET_DELETE saga (steps 12/13) already removed the DataSet entity after its teardown completed, so this usually returns `404`. It remains only as a safety net for a never-provisioned dataset, which is deleted synchronously (`204`) without a saga.

  **Expected Response:** 404 Not Found (already removed by the DELETE saga). 204 only for a never-provisioned run.
}
